/-!
# Decay of g(E₄²E₆)^m against hΔ^m at the cusps

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.eventually_norm_slash_le_of_isIntegral_adjoin_coeffEmb_jq_inv_pow`
(`5991adb3-f9e2-56b1-a149-d155a61b3080`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `2875a369-3dff-5b65-afe5-d5211ce2c4c6`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Fix $N \in \mathbb{N}$, a weight $k \in \mathbb{Z}$ and $m \in \mathbb{N}$ with $1 \le m$, and let
$g, h$ be modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$ with $h \neq 0$. Let $X$ be a Laurent series
over $\mathbb{C}$ satisfying $X \cdot \tilde h = \tilde g$, where $\tilde g, \tilde h$ denote the
$q$-expansions of $g$ and $h$ at period $1$, regarded as power series and then as Laurent series.
Write $j_q$ for the Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\ \mathbb{C}\ \mathrm{jq}$, that is, the
coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to \mathbb{C}$ of $q^{-1}$ times the power series
$\mathrm{jNumQ}$ (the numerator series of the $j$-invariant with rational coefficients). Let $M \in
\mathbb{N}$ and assume that $X^{2M} \, j_q^{\,mM+1} \, (j_q - 1728)^{mM}$ is integral over the
$\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated by $j_q^{-1}$. Then for every $A \in
\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and every real $\varepsilon > 0$, one has, for $\tau$ eventually in the
filter $\mathrm{atImInfty}$ on the upper half-plane,
$$\bigl\| \bigl((z \mapsto g(z)\,(E_4(z)^2 E_6(z))^m)\bigr|_{k+14m} A\bigr)(\tau) \bigr\| \le
\varepsilon \, \bigl\| \bigl((z \mapsto h(z)\,\Delta(z)^m)\bigr|_{k+12m} A\bigr)(\tau) \bigr\|,$$
the slash being the weight-$(k+14m)$, resp. weight-$(k+12m)$, action of the image of $A$ in
$\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$.

This is the analytic half of the criterion that turns integrality of $X^{2M} j^{mM+1}(j-1728)^{mM}$
over $\mathbb{C}[1/j]$ into vanishing at the cusps: the order of $X$ in the local parameter at the
cusp $A\infty$ exceeds the pole order of the relevant power of $j$, so the quotient
$g(E_4^2E_6)^m/(h\Delta^m)$ tends to $0$ there. It is used by
[`ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_cuspForm_qExpansion_eq_mul_thetaL_pow_of_isIntegral)
to produce a cusp form with prescribed $q$-expansion.

